  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "No gap in the `habeas:coverage` citation on `src/execution_coverage/progress.rs#mod[tests]/impl[RecordingTerm/indicatif::TermLike]/fn[write_line]`.\n\n- **Substantive reason:** The commentary gives a real justification, not just difficulty. The adapter is a unit-test-only `TermLike` implementation, and the trait requires `write_line` even though it is unused.\n- **Agrees with the source:** `write_line` only calls `self.write_str(&format!(\"{text}\\n\"))`. `write_str` in the same impl (`fn[write_str]`) is the recording path that indicatif renders through. It pushes to `text` and `frames`, and tests such as `stage_and_conversion_counts_are_visible_then_cleared` exercise it.\n- **Scope:** The item sits inside `mod[tests]`, so no application input can reach it.\n- **PTY claim holds:** The PTY claim is supported by `tests/execution_coverage.rs#fn[coverage_progress_on_a_pty_preserves_reports_and_plain_output_policy]`. It opens a real PTY with `openpty` and asserts on the progress output. `tests/authoring_batch.rs` also has PTY tests for other output.\n- **Form:** The citation is a fenced commentary on an explicit function with a body. That is a permitted use of the built-in.",
